7. Entry and Exit Criteria
Entry Criteria
Testing may begin when:
1. Test environment is available and stable.
2. Required application build is deployed.
3. Approved requirements/testable acceptance criteria are available.
4. Required user accounts and permissions are available.
5. Required test data is available.
6. Required integrations are accessible.
7. Defect-management mechanism is available.
8. Test cases/scenarios for prioritized requirements are reviewed.
9. Known environment limitations are documented.
Exit Criteria
Testing may be considered complete when:
1. 100% of approved planned high-priority test cases have execution
status recorded.
2. All critical/high-priority requirements have planned coverage.
3. No open Severity 1/Critical defects remain, unless explicitly accepted by
the authorized stakeholder.
4. Remaining defects have documented severity, impact, workaround/status,
and disposition.
5. Regression testing for the agreed release scope is completed.
6. Required integration scenarios are completed.
7. Applicable non-functional tests are completed.
8. Test summary report is prepared.
9. Business/product stakeholders approve known residual risks.
Note: The numerical thresholds above are proposed acceptance criteria
because the PRD does not define test completion thresholds, defect tolerances,
or ownership.
