11. Suspension and Resumption Criteria
Suspension Criteria
Testing may be suspended if:
Test environment becomes unavailable or unstable.
Critical functionality required for further testing is blocked.
Required test accounts/access are unavailable.
Required test data is unavailable.
A critical defect prevents meaningful continuation.
Major dependency/integration services are unavailable.
Application build is changed significantly during active execution without an
agreed regression strategy.
Resumption Criteria
Testing may resume when:
Environment is restored and validated.
Blocking defect is fixed or an approved workaround is available.
Required access/data is restored.
Dependencies are available.
New build is deployed and smoke testing passes.
Impacted test cases are identified and regression scope is agreed.
